 "reasons": "Both claimed fixes hold. In g1, sc_gale_exposure's start now stages an unroofed organic, a roofed organic and an unroofed mechanoid in one Gale, with each pawn's roof state asserted. Its expect requires RM_GaleDeafened on the unroofed organic only. Control Arm B (a deafen hook that ignores roof and mechanoid status) must be rejected. This matches the real gate at RM_WindCalendar.cs:85 (`p.Dead || p.RaceProps.IsMechanoid || p.Position.Roofed(map)` → continue). In g2, sc_cuts' control adds a third arm, a vaporator that dries or converts terrain, which the checker must reject. So a check blind to drying scars no longer passes. This matches the 'Plain vaporator, no scar' card ruling at RM_WindVaporator.xml:6. The changed entries open no new gap. Both scenes still meet the contract: acceptance kind, staged by a script, a named entry_point with an entry_point_item filed because the entry point is missing, asserted start, a control with rules_out, recovery and hold. The exam-reuse decision changes no scene or bar. bark_wardens_removed and farmer_camps_removed are covered by sc_cuts' expect and its guardian and farmerFaction control arms. No proof is claimed; the scenes are planned and their entry points not yet built, which this coverage judgment does not require.",
